      "content": "#include <cstdio>\n#include <vector>\n#include <climits>\n\nstatic inline int nextInt() {\n    static const int BUFSIZE = 1 << 20;\n    static char buf[BUFSIZE];\n    static int idx = 0, size = 0;\n    int sign = 1;\n    int x = 0;\n    while (true) {\n        if (idx >= size) {\n            size = fread(buf, 1, BUFSIZE, stdin);\n            idx = 0;\n            if (size == 0) return -2147483648;\n        }\n        char c = buf[idx++];\n        if (c >= '0' && c <= '9') {\n            x = c - '0';\n            while (true) {\n                if (idx >= size) {\n                    size = fread(buf, 1, BUFSIZE, stdin);\n                    idx = 0;\n                    if (size == 0) break;\n                }\n                c = buf[idx];\n                if (c < '0' || c > '9') break;\n                idx++;\n                x = x * 10 + (c - '0');\n            }\n            return sign * x;\n        } else if (c == '-') {\n            sign = -1;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nstatic inline long long maxWindow(const std::vector<long long>& arr, int len, int window) {\n    long long cur = 0;\n    for (int j = 0; j < window; ++j) cur += arr[j];\n    long long mx = cur;\n    for (int j = window; j < len; ++j) {\n        cur += arr[j] - arr[j - window];\n        if (cur > mx) mx = cur;\n    }\n    return mx;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n = nextInt();\n    int s = nextInt();\n\n    std::vector<int> mat((size_t)n * n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        size_t rowBase = (size_t)i * n;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            mat[rowBase + j] = nextInt();\n        }\n    }\n\n    std::vector<long long> colSum(n, 0);\n    for (int i = 0; i < s; ++i) {\n        size_t rowBase = (size_t)i * n;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            colSum[j] += mat[rowBase + j];\n        }\n    }\n\n    long long best = maxWindow(colSum, n, s);\n\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n - s; ++i) {\n        size_t exitRowBase = (size_t)(i - 1) * n;\n        size_t enterRowBase = (size_t)(i + s - 1) * n;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            colSum[j] -= mat[exitRowBase + j];\n            colSum[j] += mat[enterRowBase + j];\n        }\n        long long curBest = maxWindow(colSum, n, s);\n        if (curBest > best) best = curBest;\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", (int)best);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Flattening the matrix into a contiguous array and replacing the snake-window O(S*N^2) algorithm with an O(N^2) column-sum sliding window improves cache locality and reduces redundant arithmetic, yielding significant speedup.",
  "notes": "The new implementation stores the matrix as a flat int vector for contiguous memory access. It computes column sums for the first S rows, then slides the top row while updating all column sums in O(N) per step. A linear scan over colSum finds the best horizontal window of length S. Total time is O(N^2) with only O(N) extra space beyond the matrix itself. Fast input via fread reduces I/O overhead.",
